# Gate step 1587-qqzs — a TERM cleans up test-awk-float-lc-numeric's mutants
# before the preflight door's KILL. The door signals only the guard pid (no
# setsid on darwin): TERM, a 1 s grace, then KILL. The script writes three
# .mutant-lcnum-* copies BESIDE the producers, and pre-fix its EXIT trap was
# deferred behind a producer running in $(...), so a deadline kill leaked them
# into the checkout. The fixture TERMs the real script while a sed shim holds
# its first producer, and has a constructed pre-fix-shape control that must
# leak. A mutant already present before the run is could-not-run, never a pass.
#
# STEP_LUA is a LITERAL path on purpose (1063-nraf).
